---
description: Rules for AI-assisted development — always apply
alwaysApply: true
---

## Always

1. Follow Clean Architecture + MVVM/MVI (Intent / State / Effect / ViewModel / UseCase / Repository)
2. XML + View Binding only — never Compose, never Data Binding, never `findViewById`
3. Use the project's DI framework — register new bindings in the composition root
4. Use Version Catalog — no hardcoded dependency versions
5. Respect module boundaries — presentation must not depend on `:data`
6. Put **all** user-facing strings in the single shared strings file (e.g. `:core-ui`) — no hardcoded UI strings
7. Match existing naming conventions (resources, packages, classes)
8. Add unit tests for new UseCases and ViewModels when adding features
9. Use proper dispatchers (`IO` / `Default`) — assume lists/files may have thousands of items; never block Main
10. Log with `Constants.TAG*` and format `ClassName: functionName: State: details`
11. Support **portrait and landscape** for all UI screens
12. Do heavy mapping in Repository / UseCase; `toUi()` in ViewModel only when needed (with dispatcher if heavy)

## Never

1. Never add libraries without explicit human approval
2. Never add Hilt/Dagger/Compose/RxJava unless project already uses them
3. Never put business logic or heavy mapping in Fragments/Activities/Adapters beyond render + intent dispatch
4. Never access DataSources directly from presentation
5. Never skip `android:exported` on manifest components with intent-filters
6. Never use `GlobalScope` for feature work
7. Never modify unrelated files when implementing a feature
8. Never do heavy mapping/sorting/IO on the Main thread
9. Never invent ad-hoc log tags — use `Constants.TAG*`
10. Never lock the app to one orientation unless product explicitly requires it

## New feature checklist

- [ ] Feature package: `{di,intent,state,effect,viewModel,ui}` (+ adapter/mapper as needed)
- [ ] Extend `Parent*` / `Base*` UI bases; layouts work in **portrait and landscape**
- [ ] Domain UseCase(s) + repository interface if new capability needed
- [ ] Data repository impl + DataSource if needed (heavy work / DTO mapping off Main)
- [ ] Mapping: Repo/UseCase for heavy work; `toUi()` in ViewModel if needed — not in UI classes
- [ ] DI: `lazyModule` + register in composition root (`KoinModules`)
- [ ] Strings in the **single** shared strings file (+ translations)
- [ ] Logs use `Constants.TAG*` with class/function/state format
- [ ] Permissions via Intent → Effect → base permission helper when needed
- [ ] Analytics event via shared EventsProvider when screen should be tracked
- [ ] ProGuard packages covered if new `state`/`intent`/`effect`/`model` types
- [ ] Unit tests for UseCase / ViewModel
- [ ] Verify no `:presentation` → `:data` dependency
- [ ] Large-list path: `ListAdapter` + DiffUtil / background mapping considered
- [ ] If ads/premium: gate on entitlement + RC; use existing managers — not raw SDK in Fragments